# Applies to backend/Dockerfile, whose build context is the repository root.
# (A plain .dockerignore in this folder is never read for a root context.)
#
# Allowlist: send only what the Dockerfile copies. Everything else — .env,
# credentials.json, sample-uploads/, the frontend build, .venv — stays out of
# the build context, so it can never reach an image by accident.
*
!backend/app
!backend/scripts
!backend/pyproject.toml
!backend/uv.lock

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
